// SLICE-PLANNER. One decision set, declared once in the ontology language.
// csfc reads this block and emits its Go projection (slice_planner.go): the
// ordered decisions a dispatch pass makes about one queued slice. A golden
// test pins the emitted Go against the checked-in file, and that comparison is
// the harness's first self-hosting stage: the emitter's output equals the
// hand-written golden, so stage 1 and stage 2 are the same bytes for the
// planner.
//
// The kind is slice_planner; the instance is dispatch_waiting. Its decisions are
// the closed set a dispatch pass checks, in order, when a queued slice does not
// run. The order is the switch in services/dispatch/graph.go's waiting:
// depends_on, held, contends, paused, rate, capacity, next_pass.

slice_planner dispatch_waiting {
  decision depends_on;
  decision held;
  decision contends;
  decision paused;
  decision rate;
  decision capacity;
  decision next_pass;
}
